  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HCFC phase-out management plan (Stage II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Iraq will freeze its consumption of HCFCs by 1 January 2013 at the level of 1,858.18 mt (102.2 ODP tonnes) and gradually reduce it from the baseline data to meet a 13.82 per cent reduction in 2015. The overarching strategy of Iraq has been based on consumption reductions in the servicing sector through the enforcement of regulatory measures, recovery/recycling, and better practices to reach the set 2015 compliance target.</narrative>
  </description>
